  "notes": "Modified cash basis, treated as cash. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column (p6, right half of the statement); the Eliminations column removes interfund transfers (General to Depreciation 275,000 inside Pupil transportation, General to Activity 50,000 inside Extracurricular, Student Fees to General 53,339), so transfers_in/out are null and the total column ties (12,199,289 and 11,060,355; roll-forward 8,797,986 + 12,199,289 - 11,060,355 = 9,936,920). Beginning cash = beginning total fund balance 8,797,986 (p6); ending cash = total assets of governmental funds balance sheet (cash plus county treasurer cash, p4). Business-type = Nutrition Fund (p7-8): receipts are the four operating receipt lines plus nonoperating interest 9,276 (printed total only for operating, so total 324,062 is computed); roll-forward 330,698 + 324,062 - 319,797 = 334,963; measure recorded as cash because the modified cash statement's net position equals cash. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position total column (p1). Detail: General, Depreciation, Building, Bond budget schedules (pp9-12) and combining other funds (p13). The General Fund budget schedule is used for General Fund detail (statement p5-6 is not repeated as detail); the hidden 275,000 transfer to Depreciation is split out of Pupil transportation 865,415 and the 50,000 Activity transfer is an other financing line, both inside the printed total disbursements. Transfer cross-check: Activity transfer in 50,000 matches; Student Fees transfer out 53,339 matches General transfer in; Depreciation transfer in 275,000 matches the hidden pupil transportation elimination. Building and Bond budgeted interfund transfers of 525,000 had zero actual. Read pages 1-13 of 13"
